  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Roast cauliflower: Preheat the oven to 200C. Line an oven tray with baking paper. Cut the cauliflower into 2cm florets. Put the hemp seeds in a large bowl. Combine 2 tsp harissa seasoning and 1 tbs olive oil in a separate large bowl, add the cauliflower and toss to coat, then roll in the hemp seeds. Put the cauliflower on half of the lined tray and roast for 15 mins.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/146946/photos/large/prep_ingredients-ab3beb214a0a45732e4e3270dcdd8697.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Meanwhile, crush 1 garlic clove. Rinse the sprouts and pat dry with paper towel. Tear or cut the bread rolls into 3cm chunks.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/146947/photos/large/roast_cauliflower-ee5f96c73ac00fcf6fcd03b7f500abe1.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make dressing: Put 1 tsp honey and 3 tsp boiling water in a large bowl and stir to dissolve. Add the yoghurt, garlic, 1 tbs white wine vinegar and 1 tbs olive oil and stir to combine.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/146948/photos/large/toast_croutons-0974e77e1a6b9ac4bde4acd2f4a71eb4.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Toast croutons: Spread the torn bread over the other half of the tray and spray or brush with olive oil. Roast for a further 3-5 mins until the cauliflower is tender and the bread is toasted.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/146949/photos/large/make_dressing-c2bcb50f0f0650f7d5a382a7df7ee3d6.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Add the roasted cauliflower, croutons, salad leaves and sprouts to the dressing and toss to combine. Divide among bowls and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/146950/photos/large/serve_up-a633f5b989c9b04f2ec14def5de278c9.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Did you know?: Although hemp seeds are from the same species as cannabis, in this form they won't get you high. Hemp seeds are a great source of plant-based protein (even better than chia seeds) and rich in vitamins, minerals, fibre and heart-healthy fats.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/146951/photos/large/make_it_yours-1c0236a790a51710a3a0c113b3bb7ac5.jpeg"
    }
  ]
